{"overview":"This early Chaplin film has him playing a character quite different from the Tramp for which he would become famous. He is a rich, upper-class gentleman whose romance is endangered when his girlfriend oversees him being embraced by a maid. Chaplin's romantic interest in this film, Minta Durfee, was the wife of fellow Keystone actor, Roscoe \"Fatty\" Arbuckle.","cast":[{"n":"Charlie Chaplin","c":"Mr. Dovey","p":"/lRI9Ky1SMOehn04OqhYJ5hQfgIK.jpg","q":"Q882"},{"n":"Edgar Kennedy","c":"Butler","p":"/oA8h7AdAUZYg5uO0xzFMQOkc9DQ.jpg","q":"Q714724"},{"n":"Minta Durfee","c":"The Lady","p":"/8QgdVcTIocr6xdnD0lxhOBPAfUs.jpg","q":"Q443110"},{"n":"Eva Nelson","c":"Maid","p":null,"q":null},{"n":"Glen Cavender","c":"Bearded Doctor (uncredited)","p":"/mkCWTmyWtInbtNiSkBaUU20DgXz.jpg","q":"Q3108668"},{"n":"William Hauber","c":"Gardener (uncredited)","p":null,"q":"Q3568687"},{"n":"Bert Hunn","c":"Tall Ambulance Attendant (uncredited)","p":null,"q":"Q2899187"},{"n":"Harry Russell","c":"Bald Doctor (uncredited)","p":null,"q":"Q18421212"},{"n":"Billy Gilbert","c":"Short Ambulance Attendant","p":null,"q":"Q2903632"},{"n":"Chester Conklin","c":"","p":null,"q":"Q1070698"}],"country":["United States"],"wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cruel,_Cruel_Love","qid":"Q762380","rel":{"GB":{"d":"1914-06-30","c":"U"},"US":{"d":"1914-03-26","c":"NR"}},"backdrops":["/ena8cqMjEs19oRketkIFtbKHcAv.jpg","/hI1DEC52RaMpCKbb7DWt82J3pFa.jpg"]}